From 24a60ef2d4a69029ec1794253a13ca12df350792 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pablo Fontanilla <pfontani@redhat.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 13:44:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] podman-etcd: scope sync to etcd filesystem only

Bare `sync` issues sync(2), which flushes dirty buffers for every
mounted filesystem. When ODF is installed, CephFS kernel mounts block
indefinitely if Ceph is unreachable (e.g. during upgrade reboot),
causing Pacemaker's start timeout to loop.

Use `sync -f` (syncfs(2)) scoped to the etcd data directory so only
the filesystem containing /var/lib/etcd is flushed.

Resolves: OCPBUGS-104449

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 heartbeat/podman-etcd | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/heartbeat/podman-etcd b/heartbeat/podman-etcd
index bad94aa44..6142724e5 100755
--- a/heartbeat/podman-etcd
+++ b/heartbeat/podman-etcd
@@ -705,7 +705,7 @@ wipe_data_folder_for_learner()
 		ocf_log err "could not delete etcd member directory ($ETCD_MEMBER_DIR), error code: $?"
 		return $OCF_ERR_GENERIC
 	fi
-	sync
+	sync -f "$OCF_RESKEY_config_location"
 	return $OCF_SUCCESS
 }
 
